l hold every skill description to the declared description floor: the descriptions it ships are at or above it, and its skills-index check fails, naming the skill, on any description shorter than it.\" The failing case becomes a response qualifier after the `shall`, which is its honest place here, since what the row obliges is the floor, not a fault-triggered reaction alone. The acceptance, the Rationale, LLR-281 and TC-291 stay as they are, and the record needs no rewrite because the row's subject and lens are unchanged.\n\nThen re-sit SR-224 for first approval, still as the Done-when's first act.\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=first-approval\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014mVP2WRUWsWxWzD5BwfyUN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
